target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestEveryDerivationRefusesAPoisonedRun'
expect: no line in `derivations`
why:    the rule this test exists for: a derivation added without a line in `derivations` is unguarded by the refusal check AND almost certainly by the catalog, which is how the hand-enumerated pair this replaced would have let a third one through. Found by SHAPE, so the new method does not have to be remembered — it has to be declared. The mutation adds a real derivation (`Spend`, the agent sum two functions already compute inline) rather than a stub, because a stub is a defect nobody would write.
--- old
// GateOK are the statuses
--- new
// Spend is the agents this run spent. Added by a mutation entry to check that an
// unlisted derivation is reported; it duplicates a sum two callers compute inline.
func (r *Run) Spend() (int, error) {
	var n int
	for _, c := range r.Cycles {
		if c.Agents != nil {
			n += *c.Agents
		}
	}
	return n, nil
}

// GateOK are the statuses
